d 'DATADICTIONARY': module to generate an enhanced, over-time-ready codebook for multi-wave data
d
d  A modern descsave. datadictionary builds an Excel codebook that
d puts each variable's statistics, % missing, distinct count,
d common values, labels, and notes side by side (one row per
d variable, or per variable-wave over time), including the
d char[source] provenance stamp written by srctag and combineall.
d Results go to the screen, a machine-readable .dta, and a
d multi-sheet workbook, with clickable links to open them. For a
d study run in waves, files() / folder() stack a per-wave row per
d variable and add a "changed" column flagging any variable whose
d label or category set shifted since the previous wave (only
d detectable from the original wave files, since stitching destroys
d per-wave value labels). In-memory mode can also write a
d capture-guarded relabel do-file (dofile()) that re-applies
d labels, formats, notes, and chars after a CSV/Excel round-trip
d through another package, with a re-ingestion receipt, plus an
d optional infile dictionary (dictionary()). 
d
d KW: codebook; data documentation; data management; Excel
d
d Requires: Stata version 16.0
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261116
d
d Author: Eric Booth, Texas 2036
d Support: email eric.a.booth@@gmail.com
d
d Author: Elizabeth Teas, Far Harbor, LLC
d Support: email elizabeth@@farharbor.com
d
f datadictionary.ado
f ../_/_dd_open.ado
f datadictionary.sthlp
